1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:04,700
Start with the work that matters to your shop.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,700
The workspace connects your next steps with the right tools and context.

3
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:15,600
Start from a CSV, describe the products you need, or provide a source URL.

4
00:00:15,900 --> 00:00:21,700
Review the prepared catalogue in a private workspace before publishing selected products.

5
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:27,600
An agent can prepare related catalogue and content changes as one task.

6
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:33,700
Inspect the results, follow their links and review what will change.

7
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:39,600
Shape the standard storefront directly in its visual preview.

8
00:00:39,900 --> 00:00:45,700
Edit components and content, or ask the agent to prepare a design change.

9
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:51,600
Shoppers can describe what they need and compare actual products.

10
00:00:51,900 --> 00:00:57,700
Product images, prices and stock lead into the native cart and checkout.

11
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:04,200
Combine app-owned materials, custom dimensions and surcharges with company purchasing.

12
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:08,000
A separate approver reviews the exact configuration before the buyer can purchase.

13
00:01:08,300 --> 00:01:11,700
Saved inputs support reordering, while completed orders retain their purchased configuration.

14
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:18,200
Preview fictional customer profiles based on the selected catalogue and channel.

15
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:22,000
Run bounded scenarios and inspect each native action and purchase result.

16
00:01:22,300 --> 00:01:25,700
This tests API purchase journeys; it does not predict conversion or replace usability testing.

17
00:01:26,200 --> 00:01:30,600
From catalogue preparation to storefront design, purchasing and scenario testing.

18
00:01:30,900 --> 00:01:35,700
Try a standard shop or explore Veyndo with Storyfront.
